WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.464
(gentle melodic music)

00:00:01.464 --> 00:00:03.030
- [David] When we first moved here,

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.377
people thought we were crazy.

00:00:04.377 --> 00:00:05.370
- [Lise] There's a reason why

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.940
there's not a lot of
farms here in Minnesota;

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.820
it's not much soil; the climate is harsh.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.690
- [David] We knew the land could produce;

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.602
we figured we'd figure it out.

00:00:15.602 --> 00:00:17.395
(melodic orchestral music)

00:00:17.395 --> 00:00:18.930
- [Narrator] This Great Big Story

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.493
was made possible by Horizon Organic.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.805
- I'm Lise Abazs. This is
my husband, David Abazs,

00:00:32.805 --> 00:00:36.470
and we are off grid organic
farmers in Finland, Minnesota.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.648
- [David] Finland is a small community

00:00:39.648 --> 00:00:42.478
along the North Shore of Lake Superior.

00:00:42.478 --> 00:00:46.373
We've been farming this land
for the last 30 plus years.

00:00:47.549 --> 00:00:50.160
People had said you can't farm in Finland;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.453
the soil was both
infertile and challenging.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.870
You can't get a shovel into the ground

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.910
'cause it's full of rocks.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:02.400
- But it didn't matter;
everything, it just felt right.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.290
The soil, industrial farming

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.850
treats it as a medium to grow crops;

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.220
you insert the nutrients,
and the crop growers,

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.020
but organic farming focuses

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.351
on making that soil its
own living organism.

00:01:14.351 --> 00:01:17.290
You have healthy soil, you
end up with healthy plants;

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.720
and so we focused on making sure

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.006
we were feeding the soil,
not just the plants.

00:01:21.006 --> 00:01:22.570
- [David] This is all good soil;

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:25.275
it starts to get a little denser here.

00:01:25.275 --> 00:01:29.430
Through time, through compost,
through cover crops and care,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:33.150
we're able to see results,
and now the fertility

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.523
is so much greater than it's ever been.

00:01:36.537 --> 00:01:40.939
(melodic orchestral music)

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:44.640
- [Lise] Our growing season
can be as short as 33 days.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.960
In the spring we grow lots
of greens, we have lettuce,

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.377
spinach, kale, we have radishes and beets.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:55.014
- We need water, we need
food, we need energy;

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:58.660
we have tried to figure out
how do we do all of those.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:03.280
Everything we run is from
solar and wind power.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.400
Our water is pumped from the Earth;

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.280
we use a compost toilet.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.580
- [Lise] And of course, you know,

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.240
what homestead would be complete

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.453
without a flock of free range chickens?

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.730
Most of what we grow is
distributed to customers

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:20.040
through a CSA, which is
Community Supported Agriculture.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.760
It's a way for small farmers

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.520
to get dependable sales of their products.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.050
We sell about 50 shares,

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:29.162
which can feed a couple of 100 people.

00:02:29.162 --> 00:02:31.670
- [David] For many years
we've been involved

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:34.670
in the social fabric in the community,

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.899
so we installed solar at the fire station

00:02:36.899 --> 00:02:38.900
and then the community center,

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:42.310
so that that was all part
of kind of mainstreaming

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.996
renewable energy into our community.

00:02:44.996 --> 00:02:47.600
- [Lise] Sharing what we've
learned by living this way

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.763
will hopefully make the world better.

00:02:56.496 --> 00:02:59.663
(light melodic music)

